one million subscribers a youtube  milestone i never expected to reach but  here's the story of how i got here in  2017 i started the channel with no video  editing skills and zero expectations i  hated the sound of my own voice and have  been told i have the personality of a  carrot but i was like screw it i'm going  to try youtube and probably fail and  disappoint my mom again in the process i  found there was a need for developer  content around angular and firebase so i  created some really bad videos that were  very useful to this highly specialized  audience welcome to angularfirebase you  create a new app with the angular cli  then these files are going to be here by  default i even remember my very first  comment that motivated me to keep  pushing forward in the early game the  key is to find a specialized unmet need  in the market then create the useful  educational content that audience is  looking for if you're consistent  uploading a new video say once a week  that should take you to about 10 000  subscribers in about a year or so but  then you'll hit a ceiling by the mid  game my video editing skills were much  improved to grow further i created  videos targeted at a wider audience my  first real banger was firebase basics my  philosophy has always been to make the  next video better than the last one it  takes a lot of time and experimentation  to really optimize the content for what  your audience is looking for listen to  feedback and give the audience what they  want like i don't show my face in my  videos because my handsomeness is  distracting and it forces me to find  useful graphics that actually represent  what i'm talking about what you don't  want to do is copy somebody else not  only will that eat away at your soul but  in order to grow on youtube you really  need to find the thing that makes you  unique to reach 100k subscribers it took  675 days and 150 uploads the late game  is where things get difficult you'll be  extremely burned out at this point and  10xing the road to 100k might seem  impossible to keep growing though the  formula is simple keep uploading and  keep getting better at this point i  started taking a more scientific  approach by optimizing two metrics the  click-through rating and the watch time  to optimize clicks you need a good title  and thumbnail that's more of an art form  than anything you need to know what your  audience wants and how to surprise them  with something creative for me that  comes easy because i also have a lot of  fun and get really excited about every  video i create for watch time i have a  formula with three ingredients most  importantly the content needs to be  educational and useful the second  ingredient is storytelling there are so  many interesting stories to tell about  the history of software and the people  behind it the final ingredient is humor  i can tell jokes that are actually  encoded messages of things that i  couldn't say otherwise without sounding  like a total dick this has been how to  get 1 million youtube subscribers in 100  seconds and i want to send a huge thank  you to everybody who supported my  channel over the years it truly means  more to me than you'll ever know i've  learned so much met amazing people and  have the rare privilege of actually  enjoying what i do for work and now we  get to start down the road to 10 million  i'm not sure how we'll get there yet but  we will get there or die trying thanks  for watching and i will see you in the  next one  [Music]
 

